+## Assignment execution authority
+
+In assignment mode, only the worker may start a stage on an opted-in repository.
+It supplies an immutable GitHub execution token, worker mapping, issue/stage,
+review-handoff ID and integration-turn token where required. A stable lane alone
+cannot admit duplicate sessions. The worker launches the same role programs,
+pinned prompts and tool scopes; no model receives discovery credentials or a new
+GitHub/mutation tool.
+
+Job entry, ops and credentialed writer/push boundaries reread current scope and
+grants. The current manifest/config, signed state, live claim, execution ref and
+bound review ownership must agree. Observed unassignment, closure, cancellation,
+reassignment, input changes or scope removal holds newly unauthorized work. A
+request consumed by its reviewer's corresponding submission is not cancellation.
+These checks observe GitHub; they do not make concurrent external changes atomic.
+
+Before a guarded mutation, signed state records intent. A code/private-wiki
+checkpoint records only remotely confirmed heads, branch, PR and input revision.
+The developer saves a bound handoff before requesting review. Acceptance remains
+in signed state after request consumption, including across worker replacement.
+It never substitutes for hardening, actual approval, exact-result verification or
+postmerge security clearance. Public wiki publication and issue completion retain
+their existing guards.
+
+Uncertain outcomes retain their pending intent and execution fence. A stopped
+worker reports local-only recovery rather than publishing refused bytes to make
+them appear recoverable. Required patches, bundles, mirrors and checkouts remain
+recovery evidence, not another scheduler or permission to push. A replacement
+holds if it cannot prove a checkpoint or lacks required unpublished work.
+
+The operator must prove the old executor stopped and reconcile writes/evidence
+before releasing stale refs; lease expiry does not suffice. SIGINT/SIGTERM ends
+and awaits only the worker's owned stage process group. See the
+[worker operating guide](https://github.com/axolotl-logic-io/ecosystem/blob/main/apps/issue-pipeline/README.md#assignment-driven-workers-opt-in)
+for scope, retry timing and quiescent cutover with **#60**. Legacy adoption remains
+**#58**; this contract installs or starts nothing.
+
