+## Assignment-driven workers
+
+### `github-is-the-worker-coordination-store`
+
+Assignment mode is an operator opt-in, not a change to the installed runtime.
+The [worker operating guide](https://github.com/axolotl-logic-io/ecosystem/blob/main/apps/issue-pipeline/README.md#assignment-driven-workers-opt-in)
+defines the non-secret manifest and repository settings. Worker IDs map to the
+configured development or review/merge GitHub account, separately from models and
+private credentials. The manifest allows repositories explicitly; ecosystem and
+project-buddy keep independent target bases, checks, trusted humans and wikis.
+
+Workers paginate assignments, PR requests and authenticated issue/PR event history.
+New development needs an allowed human collaborator as author and a current grant
+from the configured review/merge account or an allowed human collaborator. An
+assignee list, label or visitor request cannot establish provenance. The developer
+may request review only for the issue's recorded PR and confirmed checkpoints.
+Review scans signed handoffs as well as pending requests, so accepted ownership
+survives GitHub consuming a request during that reviewer's bound submission.
+
+Signed v2 coordination adds worker/status, reason, heartbeat/retry timing,
+checkpoints, handoff and pending mutation intent to existing stage/receipt state.
+Handoffs bind their own ID, assignment and request events, source/private-wiki
+heads, branch, PR and trusted inputs. Snapshots exclude prior reviews/events,
+including signals with the same timestamp. Bound changes requests or a new
+assignment back to development invalidate old hardening/integration/security
+permission. Review feedback remains operational evidence, not human input.
+
+Question, prerequisite, split-parent, stop, role, legacy, approval and mutation
+gates remain in force. Changed trusted requirements return development to Author.
+Same-repository prerequisites use `<!-- agent-pipeline:after 12,34 -->` and must
+be closed and completed or marked `agent:merged`. A held issue does not prevent
+other eligible assigned work. The worker never splits or self-assigns issues.
+
+### `exclusive-workers-and-reconciled-recovery`
+
+GitHub create-if-absent refs exclude duplicate executors, including two instances
+sharing one worker identity. `pipeline-execution/issue-N` names an immutable token;
+the stage's claim lane includes that token. `pipeline-integration/HEX_BASE` holds
+one repository/base integration-to-completion turn. Existing signed claims still
+supply leases and bounded heartbeat comments. These are cooperating-worker
+controls, not atomic exclusion of outside GitHub actors.
+
+Mutation intent precedes source/private-wiki pushes, PR creation, review requests,
+code merge, public wiki publication and completion. Confirmation precedes clearing
+the intent. Only an exact remote observation becomes a recoverable checkpoint.
+A lost response or save retains the intent and execution ref. There is no blind
+write retry or automatic stale-fence deletion. Lease expiry alone never proves an
+old process stopped or its write did not land.
+
+Before stale takeover, the operator must terminate the prior owner, reconcile
+remote branches/PRs and genuine receipts, preserve required local evidence and
+restore current authority. Missing local patches, bundles, mirrors or checkouts
+can require a hold. A checkpoint does not claim those unpublished bytes exist on
+GitHub. New scope, claim, assignment or request loss refuses subsequent controlled
+actions; it does not authorize salvage pushes or concurrent replacement.
+
+### `bounded-assignment-polling`
+
+A worker continues after idle and completed sweeps. Healthy polling defaults to
+60 seconds; configured exponential backoff is capped, except that a later server
+Retry-After/reset remains a minimum. `pipeline-retry/TIMESTAMP-ID` refs preserve
+repository retry deadlines across replacement. `pipeline-discovery/WORKER` prevents
+an interrupted or unconfirmed discovery/backoff write from silently restarting.
+Pagination exhaustion is incomplete discovery, not an empty queue or unassignment.
+
+Only disposable timers live locally. A new worker reconstructs assignments,
+accepted handoffs, stages, branch bindings, checkpoints and receipts from GitHub.
+Signed state, claim heartbeats and keyed `assignment-observer` comments expose
+ownership, holds, retry times and recovery needs. Local PIDs/logs do not authorize
+progress. Read failures never imply permission to repeat uncertain mutations.
+
