 ## Cutover
 
-Cutover is quiescent, not a rolling upgrade. The exact combined code/wiki candidate must pass its source gates and fresh independent security review before operator-authorized installation or job launch ([`installed-not-merged`](#installed-not-merged)).
+Cutover is quiescent, not a rolling upgrade. Coordinate assignment operation with ecosystem **#60**; retained-legacy-state adoption remains **#58**. Source delivery does not enable configs, install files, start workers or change assignments. The exact combined code/wiki candidate must pass its source gates and fresh independent security review before operator-authorized installation or job launch ([`installed-not-merged`](#installed-not-merged)).
 
 Before installation the operator stops new dispatch, stops or drains only owned jobs, verifies their leases and processes are released, and snapshots the installation, configuration, signed state and recovery artifacts. Pushed commits, accurate checkpoints, refused local work and genuine merge/security provenance must survive. Unrecognized state or uncertain delivery requires explicit reconciliation, not a blind restart or reset. The operator reviews the install dry-run, installs as one unit only while no old-version job runs, then pins the approved prompts and explicitly assigns work from preserved state. Never mix installed versions under live jobs; no compatibility shim solely for such coexistence is required.
 
