+
+Assignment cutover also drains explicit dispatch before enabling worker scope. Opted-in repositories refuse explicit stage jobs without worker execution authority. Do not mix modes, installed versions or overlapping owners. Existing v2 work without assignment coordination needs explicit reconciliation, not implicit adoption. Stale execution/integration/discovery refs and pending intents must be reconciled before releasing ownership; snapshots and required local recovery evidence remain necessary even though the queue is in GitHub.
